  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates which lottery has a higher probability of the minimum outcome (0 Euros), and prefers that lottery. The individual’s reasoning focuses on avoiding the outcome of 0 Euros and values a higher chance of receiving any money, which implies attention to the probability of the minimum outcome. Although the individual frames it positively (chance to gain something), this is equivalent to minimizing the chance of 0 Euros, which is the same as maximizing the probability of non-minimum outcomes — a closely related but inverse perspective. However, the core information used — the probability associated with the worst outcome — is indeed considered by the individual. The slight conceptual difference (focusing on avoiding zero vs. directly focusing on the probability of zero) does not negate the use of the same underlying information. Given the close alignment in both the information considered and the implied preference for lower risk of the worst outcome, it is highly likely the individual used reasoning consistent with the decision reason. The preference for a lower chance of 0 Euros (i.e., higher chance of positive gain) corresponds to preferring the lottery with higher probability of the minimum outcome (0 Euros) — which is Lottery A. The individual's choice aligns with this rule, and their justification centers on this trade-off.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
